The checksums are Maven Central's published ones (the .sha1 and .sha256
files beside each jar), checked against the files; each jar's .asc
signature verifies with key 0181A4828FA27B6BE6F1F5A68611CD28F472E006
(Guillaume Nodet, JLine's maintainer).

License: BSD 3-Clause (LICENSE-jline.txt, from
https://github.com/jline/jline3/blob/jline-3.30.17/LICENSE.txt). The
provider registry files inside jline-terminal and jline-terminal-ffm
(META-INF/jline/providers/*, META-INF/services/*, META-INF/jline/README.md)
carry an Apache-2.0 header; the code is BSD-3.

Source: https://github.com/jline/jline3 (tag jline-3.30.17).

Only these three are used: the reader, the terminal, and the FFM terminal
provider (it calls the C library through Java's foreign function API; the
JVM needs --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED, which the launchers and
lua.jar's manifest give). The terminal's 'stty' provider (in
jline-terminal) is the fallback. jline-terminal's POM also depends on
jline-native (JNI libraries); it is left out: its classes are loaded only
for the JNI provider and for file descriptor modes JLine does not use
here. No Jansi, JNA or JNI.

To update: change JLINE_VERSION in java/Makefile, put the new jars here,
and give their checksums above.
